# Build-context excludes for the example workbench images (context is the repo root).
# Keeps the context small and avoids copying host-only or generated trees into the build.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
.git
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/dist
**/*.db
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
apps/example/_frontend_tpl_check
# Environment files may contain secrets: compose's own variable file and its variants,
# and the rendered app-declared variables, per service too (`.app.worker.env`). The
# example images use the repository root as build context, so every one is ignored at
# any depth; the tracked examples stay.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.example.jinja
**/.app.env
**/.app.*.env
